Our hosting options include the Sovereign HDS tier on OuraneCloud, which is SecNumCloud-qualified, HDS-certified, and located within the EU, ensuring data sovereignty and compliance with regulatory requirements. We have measures in place for encryption (TLS 1.3 in transit and AES-256 at rest) and pseudonymisation of sensitive data.

Our solution provides explainable recommendations or suggestions, with source citations, retrieved passages, and a retrieval trace, allowing for a posteriori audit and ensuring transparency and traceability. We assist with drafting clinical and administrative content, such as discharge summaries and medical reports, and provide template-guided drafting for various documents.

We support continuity of care between professionals and services by providing structured handover summaries, enabling efficient resumption of handling by another professional. Our solution is designed to fit into existing practices without introducing rupture in clinical or administrative workflows, providing a non-decisional support tool that assists staff members in their daily activities.

Our approach optimizes costs while guaranteeing the expected quality of service, with a target gross margin percentage range of 25-35%. We propose using the sovereign HDS tier and the sovereign European model, which are more cost-efficient on the recurring side than premium high-availability tiers combined with top-tier proprietary inference.

We comply with GDPR requirements, including Art. 9 special-category data and Art. 28 processing agreements, as well as medical confidentiality and the HDS framework. Our solution does not require medical-device qualification (CE marking / MDR), and we have flagged CE/MDR implications where a use case could approach the medical-device threshold.

Our proposed architecture integrates with the hospital's existing information systems and user directories, ensuring high availability and response times that meet the client's requirements. We provide change-management support and staff training to ensure a smooth transition.

We contribute to reducing energy consumption by leveraging green hosting partners like OuraneCloud, which offers sovereign hosting in the EU, renewable energy, and a power usage effectiveness (PUE) of 1.2. Our solution relies on low-carbon infrastructure, aligning with the client's environmental goals and requirements.

Our proposal meets all the evaluation criteria, including quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance with regulatory requirements, level of security, data sovereignty, quality of integration with the existing SIH/DPI, total cost of the proposed solution, consideration of environmental issues, and capacity for innovation. We are committed to delivering a high-quality solution that meets the CHRB's needs and expectations.
